# CesiumJS skills are active

All 14 CesiumJS domain skills plus the orientation skill are enabled. When writing or editing CesiumJS, Cesium ion, 3D Tiles, CZML, or globe/geospatial code, read and follow every relevant skill before acting:

- `using-cesiumjs-skills` — maps the 14 domain skills; start here for CesiumJS requests
- `cesiumjs-viewer-setup` — Viewer, widgets, Ion tokens, bootstrapping a globe
- `cesiumjs-camera` — camera, flyTo, navigation constraints, entity tracking
- `cesiumjs-entities` — points/labels/models/polygons; GeoJSON/KML/CZML/GPX
- `cesiumjs-3d-tiles` — tilesets, metadata, voxels, clipping, MVT
- `cesiumjs-imagery` — base maps, imagery providers, split-screen
- `cesiumjs-terrain-environment` — terrain, atmosphere, sky, fog, lighting, shadows
- `cesiumjs-primitives` — Primitive API, batching, BufferPrimitive, GeoJsonPrimitive
- `cesiumjs-materials-shaders` — Fabric materials, IBL, post-processing, bloom
- `cesiumjs-custom-shader` — GLSL CustomShader for Model/tileset/voxels
- `cesiumjs-time-properties` — Clock, JulianDate, sampled/interval properties
- `cesiumjs-spatial-math` — Cartesian3, Matrix4, ellipsoid, projections
- `cesiumjs-interaction` — picking, hover, drag, ScreenSpaceEventHandler
- `cesiumjs-models-particles` — glTF/GLB loading, animation, particles
- `cesiumjs-core-utilities` — Resource, Color, Event, error handling

Skill files live in `.cursor/skills/cesiumjs-*/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/skills/using-cesiumjs-skills/SKILL.md`. Load the matching `SKILL.md` (and extra `.md` references such as `REFERENCE.md` or `DOMAINS.md`) instead of improvising CesiumJS setup.

Source: https://github.com/CesiumGS/cesiumjs-skills (Apache-2.0, CesiumJS v1.144).
